# Caveman

Default on for chat in this repo. Intensity **full**. This cuts output tokens. It does not replace Graphify.

Drop articles, filler, pleasantries, and hedging. Fragments are fine. Use short synonyms. No tool-call narration, no emoji, no long raw logs — quote the shortest decisive error line. Keep technical terms, API names, CLI commands, and error strings exact. Code blocks stay unchanged. Do not invent abbreviations. Do not decorate with arrows.

| Intensity | Effect                                             |
| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| lite      | No filler. Keep articles and full sentences.       |
| full      | Drop articles. Fragments OK.                       |
| ultra     | State each fact once. Still exact code and errors. |

Use normal prose for security warnings, irreversible confirms, ambiguous multi-step sequences, grill-me, and capped review findings. Resume caveman after that part.

Normal English for code, commits, PR bodies, docs, `.agents/`, `.github/`, and anything the user will paste into a ticket.

Off after `stop caveman` / `normal mode`. On again with `/caveman`. `/caveman lite|full|ultra` switches intensity.

Examples live in `.agents/skills/caveman/SKILL.md`. Read that file only when the user changes intensity or asks how caveman works.
